1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,310
The earth shook in the sea near Panama.

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:05,620
How dangerous was this earthquake? On 4 October, local time

3
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:07,320
at 8 a.m.,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:08,450
in the Pacific Ocean,

5
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:10,810
a magnitude 5.1 earthquake struck.

6
00:00:10,810 --> 00:00:12,530
Its epicentre was near the Panama–

7
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:14,640
Costa Rica border,

8
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:17,020
about two hundred

9
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:18,730
ninety-five kilometres south of Punta Burica,

10
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:20,920
only 10 km deep.

11
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,480
The good news: it was at sea, far from population centres,

12
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:27,160
so no damage, no tsunami, no danger.

13
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,840
This region is an earthquake hotspot.

14
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:32,540
In this sea area alone, in 2026, thirteen earthquakes

15
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:35,050
stronger than 4.5 have already occurred.

16
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:38,360
In 1991 a 7.4 earthquake struck here,

17
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,550
in which 23 people died.

18
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:43,120
Have you ever felt an earthquake?

19
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,660
Tell us in the comment section.

